Storybook coverage addition on branch `feature/SFCC-236_product-card-shared-component` in `/Users/marcel.a.n.navarro/Dev/zimmermann-pwa`, approved by Marcel. The Jira AC for SFCC-236 explicitly calls for "price (incl. was/now)" across the PLP, Home, Wishlist, and Recently Viewed Full History variations, but no story for `ZimmProductCardContent` currently demonstrates the was/now (sale) price state — every existing story only sets `currentPrice`, never `originalPrice`.

**File:** `overrides/app/components/ui-kits/molecules/zimmProductCardContent/index.stories.tsx` — read it in full first to match its exact conventions (it's short).

**Confirmed already:** `ZimmProductCardContent`'s `originalPrice?: string` prop is real, already wired straight through to the composed `ZimmProductPrice` atom (`index.tsx` around line 246, alongside `currentPrice` and `isLive={false}`). This component is variation-agnostic for pricing — it doesn't know or care whether it's rendering for PLP/Home/Wishlist, it just renders whatever price props it's given — so one clean story demonstrating `originalPrice`+`currentPrice` together is the right, proportionate coverage, matching how `Unavailable` and `LoadingPrice` each demonstrate one meaningful price-related state without crossing every other prop combination.

**Add one new story**, placed directly after `Default` and before `WithAttributes` (or wherever reads best given the file's existing order — use your judgement, but keep it near the other price-focused stories):

```tsx
/** Was/Now (sale) pricing: originalPrice set alongside currentPrice — the AC's "price (incl.
 *  was/now)" requirement across PLP/Home/Wishlist/Recently Viewed. Composed straight through to
 *  ZimmProductPrice, which owns the actual was/now visual treatment. */
export const WithSalePrice: Story = {
  args: {
    ...Default.args,
    currentPrice: '$416.50',
    originalPrice: '$595.00',
  },
};
```

Before finalizing, check `ZimmProductPrice`'s own component/stories (`overrides/app/components/ui-kits/atoms/zimmProductPrice/`) to confirm the exact expected relationship between `currentPrice`/`originalPrice` (e.g. does it expect `originalPrice` to always be numerically higher than `currentPrice`, any specific formatting convention, currency symbol placement) and match its own existing story fixtures' price format/values if it already has a was/now example — don't invent a mismatched or nonsensical price pair. Adjust the two price values above if needed to match that component's own established convention exactly.

**Do not touch** `Default`, `WithAttributes`, `WithAttributesOneSize`, `WithSizeChips`, `WithSizeChipsExample`, `WithSizeChipsOneSize`, `Unavailable`, `LoadingPrice`, `meta`, or any other file. This is one new, additive story only.

When done, report the exact final story code (including any price-value adjustment and why), confirm `npx tsc --noEmit` is clean, and run `npx vitest run overrides/app/components/ui-kits/molecules/zimmProductCardContent/index.test.tsx` plus the full suite to confirm no regressions. Do not stage, do not commit.

